<title>USA: Minnesota Mining to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Minnesota Mining to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minnesota Mining and Manufacturing Co said Monday the company has authorized the repurchase of up to 10 million shares of stock.  </p>
<p>The purchases are an extension of an ongoing program to reacquire shares for employee stock purchase plans and for other corporate purposes, the company said, adding that it purchased about six million shares under a previous authorization, which began February 12, 1996.</p>
<p>As of September 30, 1996, the company had 418.0 million shares outstanding, the Minnesota Mining said.</p>
<p>Minnesota Mining shares rose 1-1/4 to 81-1/4 Monday.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
